#
# Build context filter for the two repo-root images (Dockerfile → MCP server,
# Dockerfile.webapp → web app). Both are built with `.` as the context, so
# without this file the ENTIRE repository — including config/wallets.json
# (private XRPL wallet seeds), .env, and the .git history — is uploaded to the
# Docker daemon and is readable by every COPY and every RUN in the build.
#
# Deny-by-default, then re-allow only the paths the two Dockerfiles actually
# COPY. A new COPY of an unlisted path fails the build loudly ("not found in
# build context") instead of silently widening the context again.
# Both the directory and its `/**` form are re-allowed so the allowlist does
# not depend on which builder (legacy or BuildKit) expands a bare directory.

*

# ── Re-allow: dependency manifests (installed before source, for layer cache) ──
!requirements.txt
!deploy/requirements.txt

# ── Re-allow: application source ───────────────────────────────────────────
!src/
!src/**
!webapp/
!webapp/**
# Tool logic shared with the Gateway Lambdas; the MCP image copies these two
# files individually, not the whole functions/ directory.
!functions/sanctions_matcher.py
!functions/xrpl_core.py
# OFAC SDN dataset — public U.S. Treasury data, not a secret.
!data/
!data/**

# ── Never, under any circumstance, even if re-allowed above ────────────────
# config/ holds wallets.json: private XRPL seeds. Nothing in an image needs it;
# wallet material is read from Secrets Manager (xrpl-agentic-payments/wallets)
# at runtime. These rules come after the re-includes, and the last matching
# rule wins, so a future `!config/` cannot resurrect the seeds by accident.
config/
**/config/wallets.json
**/wallets.json
**/*.secret
.env
.env.*
.git/
.gitignore
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/build/
**/dist/
**/*.egg-info/
**/*.zip
cdk.out/
infra/
.claude/
.kiro/
diagrams/
docs/
scripts/
tests/
**/.DS_Store
